    {
      "title": "XSS Mental Model: Stored, Reflected, DOM",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "XSS Mental Model: Stored, Reflected, DOM",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What XSS Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Attacker data runs as ==code== in the victim's browser",
                "Runs with the page's **origin**: reads DOM, sends requests, acts as the user"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Three Types",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Stored",
                "Reflected",
                "DOM"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Payload",
                  "saved (comment, profile name)",
                  "in request (query, form field)",
                  "client source to sink"
                ],
                [
                  "Needs a click?",
                  "{green:no}",
                  "{red:yes}, crafted URL",
                  "{red:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "Server sees it",
                  "yes",
                  "yes",
                  "==often never== (#fragment)"
                ],
                [
                  "Impact",
                  "**every viewer**",
                  "one victim",
                  "one victim"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. DOM: Source to Sink",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Sources: `location.hash`, `location.search`, `document.referrer`, `postMessage`",
                "Sinks: `innerHTML`, `document.write`, `eval`, `setTimeout(string)`, `element.href`",
                "`location.hash`, `postMessage` skip the server; `location.search` is sent"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "// #<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>",
                "el.innerHTML = decodeURIComponent(location.hash.slice(1))",
                "el.textContent = decodeURIComponent(location.hash.slice(1))"
              ],
              "note": "innerHTML runs the alert; textContent is safe"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Never reaches the server?** DOM XSS via #fragment; grep for sources and sinks",
                "**Stored worse?** No crafted link; hits every viewer",
                "**Sources, sinks?** `location.hash`, `postMessage`; `innerHTML`, `eval`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Context-Aware Output Encoding",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Context-Aware Output Encoding",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Core Rule",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Encode on output==, for the **exact context** where the data lands",
                "Input validation is ==defence in depth==, not the fix",
                "Each context has its **own** encoder"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. One Encoder per Context",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Untrusted data",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Find the context",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Apply its encoder",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Output",
                    "ink": "black"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Context",
                "Encoder",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "HTML body",
                  "`< > & \" '` to entities",
                  "`&lt; &gt; &amp; &quot; &#x27;`"
                ],
                [
                  "HTML attribute",
                  "**quote** value, encode quotes",
                  "`value=\"...&quot;...\"`"
                ],
                [
                  "JS string",
                  "`\\xHH` or `JSON.stringify` in a data attribute",
                  "`\\x3c`"
                ],
                [
                  "URL parameter",
                  "`encodeURIComponent`",
                  "`a%26b`"
                ],
                [
                  "URL scheme",
                  "==allowlist== http / https",
                  "never `javascript:`"
                ],
                [
                  "CSS",
                  "its own CSS escaper",
                  "`\\3c `"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Unquoted attribute: a space breaks out, `x onmouseover=alert(1)`",
                "HTML entities do **not** stop a `javascript:` href",
                "HTML-escaping a value placed in `<script>` is the wrong encoder"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Right encoder, right context",
              "text": "==Quote== every attribute and allowlist **http/https** for URLs."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "CSP and HttpOnly Cookies as Containment",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "CSP and HttpOnly Cookies as Containment",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. CSP: Second Layer",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Response header== listing allowed script sources",
                "Limits damage when an escaping bug slips through",
                "{red:Not} a replacement for output encoding"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "http",
              "lines": [
                "Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self';",
                "  script-src 'nonce-R4nd0m' 'strict-dynamic';",
                "  object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'"
              ],
              "note": "nonce: fresh per response, unguessable"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "In script-src",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`'unsafe-inline'` (no nonce/hash)",
                  "injected inline script runs"
                ],
                [
                  "`'unsafe-eval'`",
                  "`eval()` allowed"
                ],
                [
                  "`https:`, `*.cdn.com`",
                  "any script on those hosts runs"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Inline event handlers are ==blocked== unless allowed",
                "Roll out with `Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only` + `report-to`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. HttpOnly Cookies",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==HttpOnly== hides the session cookie from `document.cookie`",
                "Add `Secure` and `SameSite=Lax` or `Strict`",
                "{red:Does NOT} stop XSS sending authenticated requests as the user"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**HttpOnly?** Stops cookie theft, not in-page requests as the user",
                "**Nonce vs allowlist?** Allowed hosts can serve usable scripts; a nonce trusts only your tags",
                "**Deploy safely?** Report-Only, fix reports, then enforce"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Framework Auto-Escaping and Its Escape Hatches",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Framework Auto-Escaping and Its Escape Hatches",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Defaults and hatches",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Escaped by default==: JSX, Angular, Vue `{{ }}`, Django, Rails",
                "Jinja2 only with ==autoescape== on (Flask does for .html)"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Hatch (escaping off)",
                "Safe"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "React",
                  "`dangerouslySetInnerHTML`",
                  "`{text}`"
                ],
                [
                  "Vue",
                  "`v-html`",
                  "`{{ }}`"
                ],
                [
                  "Angular",
                  "`[innerHTML]` + `bypassSecurityTrustHtml`",
                  "`{{ }}`"
                ],
                [
                  "Jinja2",
                  "`|safe`, autoescape off",
                  "default"
                ],
                [
                  "Django",
                  "`mark_safe`",
                  "`{{ }}`"
                ],
                [
                  "Rails",
                  "`raw`, `html_safe`",
                  "`<%= %>`"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Raw HTML? Sanitise",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Allowlist sanitiser: ==DOMPurify== (client) or a server-side equivalent",
                "Run it ==immediately before rendering==",
                "{red:Never} write your own regex filter"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "el.innerHTML = DOMPurify.sanitize(dirty)"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Still unprotected",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`href`/`src` with `javascript:` URLs",
                "`style` and event-handler attributes",
                "Server-side template injection",
                "Direct DOM writes: `ref.innerHTML`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Text positions only",
              "text": "Allowlist `http`/`https` schemes for user URLs."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Three hatches, fixes?** `v-html`, `|safe`, `mark_safe`: use default `{{ }}` escaping",
                "**Why is `<a href={userUrl}>` risky?** React 18 and earlier run `javascript:` on click; React 19 blocks it, still allowlist",
                "**Sanitiser instead of encoding?** When users must supply real HTML"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Common XSS Mistakes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Common XSS Mistakes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Filters and encoders",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Mistake",
                "Bypass",
                "Fix"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Blacklist `<script>`",
                  "`<img src=x onerror=…>`, `<svg onload=…>`, case, nested tags",
                  "Encode + allowlist"
                ],
                [
                  "Wrong context",
                  "HTML-escaped value in a JS string, unquoted attribute or URL",
                  "Encoder per exact context"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Sinks and containment",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`innerHTML`, `document.write` ==parse markup==",
                "`textContent`, `innerText` **never** do"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "el.innerHTML = userText;   // parses markup",
                "el.textContent = userText; // plain text"
              ],
              "note": "one-line fix"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "HttpOnly alone: XSS still sends requests as the user",
                "CSP alone: it is only a second layer",
                "`'unsafe-inline'` with no nonce or hash: injected inline script runs"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Useless CSP",
              "text": "Without a nonce or hash, ==unsafe-inline== lets injected inline script run, so CSP stops almost no XSS."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why does a blacklist fail?** Too many tags, events and case tricks; allowlist instead.",
                "**Fix for innerHTML with user text?** Use `textContent`.",
                "**Which mistake makes CSP useless?** `'unsafe-inline'` without a nonce or hash."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "XSS Defence Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "XSS Defence Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Three types",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Type",
                "Payload",
                "Server sees"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Stored",
                  "saved, hits ==all viewers==",
                  "yes"
                ],
                [
                  "Reflected",
                  "in the request, needs a link",
                  "yes"
                ],
                [
                  "DOM",
                  "client source to sink, e.g. `#fragment`",
                  "{red:often never}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Encode by context",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Context",
                "Encoding"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "HTML body",
                  "entities `&lt;` `&gt;` `&amp;`"
                ],
                [
                  "Attribute",
                  "==quote== it, encode quotes"
                ],
                [
                  "JS string",
                  "`\\xHH` or JSON"
                ],
                [
                  "URL",
                  "`encodeURIComponent` + http/https allowlist"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Layers, in order",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Auto-escape",
                    "sub": "templates",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Sanitiser",
                    "sub": "allowlist, rich HTML",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "CSP",
                    "sub": "nonce + strict-dynamic",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Cookies",
                    "sub": "HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Audit and interview",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "rg -n \"innerHTML|outerHTML|document\\.write|eval|dangerouslySetInnerHTML|v-html|\\|safe|mark_safe|bypassSecurityTrust\""
              ],
              "note": "sinks to grep in review"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Comment box?** Escape on output, sanitise rich HTML, nonce CSP, HttpOnly cookie",
                "**Stop and miss?** Escaping misses hatches; CSP and HttpOnly contain, they do not stop requests",
                "**Audit?** Grep sinks, trace sources to them, check CSP for `unsafe-inline`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
